  "language": "FROG",
  "title": "Evaluate named variables over three columns",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Evaluate named variables over three columns",
    "name_source": "document",
    "description": "The FROG profile stores one row per variable and one column per point. 10*a+b over rows [1,2,3] and [4,5,6] gives [14,25,36].\n\nThe FROG profile stores one row per variable and one column per point. 10*a+b over rows [1,2,3] and [4,5,6] gives [14,25,36].\n\nMode: execution. Profile: studio-draft. Capability: frog.studio.formula.evaluation@1; compiled owned-value service.\nExpected:\noutput-y_values (array<f64>) = [14,25,36]\noutput-error (cluster<\"status\":bool,\"code\":i32,\"source\":string>) = {\"status\":false,\"code\":0,\"source\":\"\"}\n",
    "author": "",
    "automatic_versioning": false,
    "program_version": "0.0.0.0",
    "tags": ["formula", "native", "typed", "independent-oracle", "example"],
    "documentation_uri": ""
